📌 Project Overview

This project analyzes the King County housing market (Seattle area) to support a fictional client, Nicole Johnson, in making an informed decision about buying a home.
The analysis includes exploratory data analysis (EDA), geographic insights, price modeling, and final home recommendations, all summarized in a presentation deck. 
The goal is to understand how location, renovations, and market patterns affect home affordability — and identify the best options for Nicole based on her budget and lifestyle.

🎯 Client Background
Nicole Johnson

Middle-budget homebuyer

Prefers lively, central neighborhoods

Values reasonable pricing and access to amenities

Wants to buy within the next 12 months


All analysis steps — cleaning, visualization, ZIP code evaluation, and suggestions — were aligned with Nicole’s preferences.

🎯 Project Goals

Assess how location influences home prices

Determine the impact of renovations on price

Evaluate whether Nicole can find an affordable home in a lively, central neighborhood

These goals structure the entire EDA process.

