🧹 Data Cleaning Summary

Float room counts (e.g., 1.7 bedrooms) → rounded to nearest whole number

Unrealistic year values (yr_renovated with extra digits) → corrected

Outlier detection for lot sizes and luxury home pricing


📊 Analysis Summary
1. Location has the strongest impact on price

Higher latitude (north) → significantly more expensive because of proximity to central Seattle

More western longitude → higher prices

Conclusion: the central–north corridor is the luxury segment.


2. Renovated homes cost more — but not proportionally

Renovated homes have higher average and median prices

Variation is large — some renovated houses are not expensive

Non-renovated homes can offer better value per square foot


3. Nicole can find mid-priced houses in central areas

ZIP codes 98168, 98106, and 98108 provide:

Reasonable distance to city center

Good housing supply

Middle-price range

Lively neighborhoods


4. Seasonal price patterns

Prices dip in late autumn and winter

Prices rise again in spring and summer
→ Best purchasing window is winter for negotiation advantage.




